# GHDL work directory and simulation binaries (rtl/sim/tg68k/run.sh).
build/

# Seed sweep artefacts: one ~3.7 MB bitstream per candidate. The measurements
# in seed_sweep/results.txt are worth keeping; the bitstreams are rebuildable
# from a seed and a commit.
seed_sweep/*.rbf
seed_sweep/*.log

# Icarus bench output. Every rtl/sim/<area>/ step compiles to a bare executable
# named tb or tb_something and tees its run to a log. CI builds these in a fresh
# checkout, so they only appear after running the suite locally -- which is
# exactly when a `git add -A` sweeps a few megabytes of binaries into a commit.
#
# The negations matter and are not tidiness: bench SOURCES are also called
# tb_*, so without them a NEW bench file would be silently ignored and pushed
# as a workflow step that compiles nothing. Already-tracked files are unaffected
# by .gitignore either way, so the damage would land on the next bench written,
# not on the ones here -- the worst kind of trap.
tb*
!tb*.v
!tb*.sv
!tb*.vh
out*.log
